body:
The pie chart shows angles representing the number of candidates who applied for admission into four programmes at a Senior Secondary School. The number of pupils who applied was 1,080. Find

(i) the angle $x^\circ$ representing the Vocational Programme;

(ii) the number of candidates who applied for the Business Programme;

(iii) correct to the nearest whole number, the percentage of the applicants who applied for the General Programme.

answer:
$$2\pi r(r + h) = 2 \times \frac{22}{7} \times 4 \times (4 + 7) = \frac{1{,}936}{7} = 276\frac{4}{7}$$

> [!answer]
> {{green:$276\dfrac{4}{7}$ cm², or about 276.57 cm²}}
